\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces RGD architecture and information flow. Query admission requires delay feasibility ($L_t$), action support ($A_t$), cost advantage ($H_t$), scene demand ($N_t$), and resource availability. At release, a returned proposal is evaluated through current-state mapping, recomputed state checks, mapped-command distinctness from the fast branch, and a proposal-specific cost margin before the shared safety projection. The optional driving-memory block was disabled in the frozen evaluations. Matched first-action rollouts from release snapshots provide offline R-VoD labels.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{4}{RGD architecture and information flow. Query admission requires delay feasibility ($L_t$), action support ($A_t$), cost advantage ($H_t$), scene demand ($N_t$), and resource availability. At release, a returned proposal is evaluated through current-state mapping, recomputed state checks, mapped-command distinctness from the fast branch, and a proposal-specific cost margin before the shared safety projection. The optional driving-memory block was disabled in the frozen evaluations. Matched first-action rollouts from release snapshots provide offline R-VoD labels}{figure.1}{}}
